WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.600 --> 00:00:05.712
Hi! Today we celebrate!

2
00:00:06.112 --> 00:00:10.536
You learn dates and write an invitation.

3
00:00:12.233 --> 00:00:17.761
These are celebrations in Germany. And this is what you say:

4
00:00:18.161 --> 00:00:21.409
Happy birthday!

5
00:00:21.809 --> 00:00:24.409
Merry Christmas!

6
00:00:24.809 --> 00:00:27.313
Happy New Year!

7
00:00:27.713 --> 00:00:30.145
Happy Easter!

8
00:00:30.545 --> 00:00:33.337
Congratulations!

9
00:00:35.033 --> 00:00:41.377
For dates you need ordinal numbers. Two are special:

10
00:00:41.777 --> 00:00:43.969
the first

11
00:00:44.369 --> 00:00:46.441
the third

12
00:00:46.841 --> 00:00:52.345
Otherwise up to nineteen: add te. Der vierte.

13
00:00:52.745 --> 00:00:58.081
From twenty: add ste. Der zwanzigste.

14
00:00:59.767 --> 00:01:04.863
When is the party? After am comes the ending en:

15
00:01:05.263 --> 00:01:07.503
On the third of May.

16
00:01:07.903 --> 00:01:10.263
But without am:

17
00:01:10.663 --> 00:01:13.431
Today is the third of May.

18
00:01:15.133 --> 00:01:19.029
Listen: Lena is having a party.

19
00:01:19.429 --> 00:01:22.413
It's my birthday soon!

20
00:01:22.813 --> 00:01:24.885
When?

21
00:01:25.285 --> 00:01:27.717
On the twelfth of May.

22
00:01:28.117 --> 00:01:30.957
Will you come to my party?

23
00:01:31.357 --> 00:01:35.541
Gladly! What should I bring?

24
00:01:35.941 --> 00:01:38.637
Maybe a salad.

25
00:01:40.333 --> 00:01:50.157
Now you! When is your birthday? Say the date: Ich habe am… Geburtstag.

26
00:01:57.867 --> 00:02:02.003
Great! Now you can:

27
00:02:02.403 --> 00:02:09.371
You say dates, congratulate and invite friends. Let's celebrate!

28
00:02:09.771 --> 00:02:11.891
See you soon!
